Subject: [PATCH 030/230] Show the YOU chip on the viewer's own leaderboard row
 only
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Leaderboards passed youLabel={t("board.you")} to every BoardRow, and
BoardRow renders the chip whenever a label exists — so all six rows on
the global board wore a YOU chip (audit DOM check: "1 D Dev YOU 170",
"2 D Demo User 2 YOU 146", …). The chip now comes from boardRowView in
lib/leaderboard.ts, which materialises the label only for row.is_you and
keeps the highlight flag in the same projection.

tests/leaderboard.test.ts renders a six-row board with exactly one
is_you row and asserts exactly one chip lands on it, that a board with
no marked row yields zero chips, and that the FA label behaves the same.
Verified live: viewer's row shows YOU, rows 2-6 show none.

